  "format": "cabid-realworld-benchmark/1",
  "limitations": [
    "ADFA-LD traces carry no timestamps, process ids, paths, or user identity. The adapter synthesises a 20-second window and a single synthetic process per trace, so CABID's ancestry, lifecycle, and rate detectors are not meaningfully exercised.",
    "The corpus is from 2013 and records 32-bit userspace syscalls. Its six attack techniques are well known and appear throughout the intrusion-detection literature, so high scores are expected and are not evidence of real-world detection quality.",
    "Only a minority of syscalls map to a CABID event class; unmapped calls are dropped. Reported event counts are therefore far smaller than trace lengths.",
    "Attack classes are small (75-338 traces each). Confidence intervals are reported because point estimates on these sizes are unstable.",
    "Traces are scored independently. ADFA-LD provides no notion of a host or a fleet, so no multi-host behaviour is measured here."
  ],
